Z||000000||fierodave||08-11-2000||08:43 PM||||<BR> <IMG SRC="http://members.theglobe.com/fierodave/gifs/paypal.gif"> <P>PAYPAL<BR>I have had a lot of email <BR>concerning my dislike with the <BR>Paypal sevice some auction sites <BR>use.  I am going to put a email <BR>here so you can get an idea why,<BR>besides my dislikes with the <BR>service I received from them, when <BR>they totally screwed up my account <BR>and told it may take a few months <BR>to fix!!!  You could also get the <BR>hundreds of emails from other Co's <BR>like I got because paypal had some <BR>personal info of mine and the <BR>endless phone calls from <BR>telemarketers I received,   I am <BR>not saying they sell your personal <BR>info, but it was right after I <BR>signed up that the mess started!  <BR>Now that I had them remove me from <BR>there system, WITH THE HELP of an <BR>attorney,  the email and phone <BR>calls stopped.  Read this email  <BR>and sorry about the long thread  <BR>but I think people should be aware <BR>of what happened to me with this <BR>paypal crap!!!<BR>This is the CO I encourage my <BR>customers to use Bidpay.com<P>Subject: BidPay - 100% PAYMENT <BR>GUARANTEE <BR>Dear BidPay Seller; <BR>We want to thank you for your past <BR>business and we most certainly <BR>look forward to being of service <BR>in the near future, we are taking <BR>the unusual step of sending this <BR>email to every one of our sellers <BR>to clarify a point that has come <BR>up and one which we have received <BR>a great deal of email about these <BR>past 3-4 days. <BR>The question is: "Does BidPay <BR>chargeback if the buyer does not <BR>pay?" <BR>The answer is a clear: "No, we DO <BR>NOT post ANY chargebacks against <BR>our sellers and all payments are <BR>100% guaranteed" <BR>Recently 'another online payment' <BR>service made a number of changes <BR>to it's Terms Of Service which <BR>require: <BR>1) That sellers surrender their <BR>bank account information and <BR>become verified. <BR>2) That if sellers refuse "Buyers <BR>will be warned that the seller (is <BR>not   verified) with their <BR>service". <BR>3) That chargebacks can now be <BR>debited to the sellers account for <BR>  disputed transactions. <BR>The changes by this 'other payment <BR>service' have prompted concerns by <BR>many of you and we thought it best <BR>to address the issue IMMEDIATELY <BR>and to clearly state our polices <BR>in PLAIN ENGLISH. <BR>1) BidPay.com DOES NOT require the <BR>seller to surrender ANY credit <BR>card or   bank information. <BR>2) BidPay.com 100% GUARANTEES <BR>PAYMENT to the seller with NO <BR>CHARGEBACKS. <BR>3) BidPay.com DOES NOT charge ANY <BR>FEE's to the seller. We never have <BR>and   we never will. <BR>4) BidPay.com DOES accept domestic <BR>as well as ALL international <BR>transactions   from buyers. "We <BR>always have" <BR>5) BidPay.com DOES NOT have ANY <BR>annual limit on the amount a <BR>purchaser may   spend. <BR>As an existing seller, you have a <BR>good understanding of how our <BR>services work, but just to quickly <BR>recap: <BR>- When a buyer places and order - <BR>we send a confirmation email to <BR>the seller to confirm the order. <BR>This email contains the buyers <BR>email address, the delivery <BR>address and all auction details. <BR>- We then review and approve the <BR>order and send a second <BR>confirmation email stating that <BR>payment is on the way. You can <BR>(and should) log into your account <BR>and verify that the order has been <BR>placed and approved. <BR>- When this second email is sent, <BR>BidPay guarantees payment to the <BR>seller with no possibility of any <BR>chargebacks. We then mail you a <BR>certified funds Western Union <BR>money order, which can be cashed <BR>at over 100,000 locations. <BR>Once again we thank you for your <BR>past business and support and look <BR>forward to being of service in the <BR>near future. <BR>BidPay.com (http://www.bidpay.com) <BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://members.theglobe.com/fierodave/gifs/fierosig.gif"> ||||reg||1
